  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"17a\"><p><strong>17a</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>As the coil is entering the magnetic field, magnetic flux linkage through the coil is changing.</p>\n<p>According to Faraday’s law of induction, the induced emf in a coil is proportional to the rate of change of magnetic flux linkage through the coil.</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"17b(i)\"><p><strong>17b(i)</strong></p><p> </p>\n<p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_04\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 4\" src=\"asset:fig_04\"/></figure>\n</p>\n<p> </p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"17b(ii)\"><p><strong>17b(ii)</strong></p><p> </p>\n<p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_05\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 5\" src=\"asset:fig_05\"/></figure>\n</p>\n<p> </p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"17c\"><p><strong>17c</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Induced emf in the coil:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\varepsilon = (0.788)(1.6 ) \\approx 1.26\"></span> V</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.26 = (94)\\times \\frac{(643 \\times 10^{-3})(2L^{2})}{386 \\times 10^{-3}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L \\approx 0.063\"></span> m or <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6.3\"></span> cm</p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A rectangular coil, moving at constant speed, enters a uniform magnetic field of strength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"643\"></span> mT at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 0\"></span>.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>a. Outline, with reference to Faraday’s law of induction, how an emf is induced in the coil.</p>\n<p>  [2]</p>\n<p>b. Sketch how the:</p>\n<p>i. magnetic flux linkage in the coil varies with time.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure>\n\n<p>ii. induced current in the coil varies with time.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_03\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 3\" src=\"asset:fig_03\"/></figure>\n\n<p>  [2]</p>\n<p>It takes the coil <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"386\"></span> ms to fully enter the magnetic field. The length of the coil is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2L\"></span>, the width of the coil is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span>, and the coil has <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"94\"></span> turns. The maximum induced current in the coil is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.788\"></span> A and the resistance of the coil is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.6 \\: \\Omega\"></span>.</p>\n<p>c. Determine <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span>. Give your answer to an appropriate number of significant figures.</p>\n<p>   [3]</p>"
  },
